  ├── Free in VG:         16 GB            ← Can extend pool by this much
  └── IF VMs fill up:     350 GB needed, only 390 GB available ⚠️

  Fix: Enable Auto-Extend

  SSH to both Proxmox hosts and edit /etc/lvm/lvm.conf:

  # Find and modify these settings:
  thin_pool_autoextend_threshold = 80    # Extend when 80% full
  thin_pool_autoextend_percent = 20      # Extend by 20%

  Or quick one-liner:
  sed -i 's/thin_pool_autoextend_threshold = 100/thin_pool_autoextend_threshold = 80/' /etc/lvm/lvm.conf
  sed -i 's/thin_pool_autoextend_percent = 20/thin_pool_autoextend_percent = 20/' /etc/lvm/lvm.conf

  Better Long-Term Fix

  Since you have NAS storage, consider moving data-heavy VMs (K8s workers with 80GB data disks) to nas-dev-data /
  nas-prod-data to free up local thin pool.

